## 5. Multiple Firecells Interactions (Table 2.3, Pages 43-44)

### 5.1 Primary Risk Group Determination (Para 1.2.2, Page 36)

#### Test Case 5.1.1: Most Onerous Requirements
**Source**: Page 36, Para 1.2.2
- **Rule**: Primary risk group = one with most onerous fire safety requirements
- **Test Cases**:
  - Firecell has CA + WB activities → Determine which is more onerous (depends on occupant load, escape height)
  - SM education (Type 7) + CA (Type 4) → SM education is more onerous
- **Implementation**: Need algorithm to determine "most onerous" based on:
  - System types required
  - FRR values
  - Other requirements

#### Test Case 5.1.2: Ancillary Activities
**Source**: Page 36, Para 1.2.2
- **Rule**: Other risk groups can be incorporated if ancillary to and support primary risk group
- **Test Cases**:
